# Pomofit Project Structure Guide

## Project Overview

Pomofit is a Next.js-based Pomodoro timer application with real-time auto-versioning, performance optimizations, and comprehensive testing.

## Core Architecture

### App Directory Structure (Next.js 13+)

- **Entry Point**: [app/page.tsx](mdc:app/page.tsx)
- **Layout**: [app/layout.tsx](mdc:app/layout.tsx)
- **Global Styles**: [app/globals.css](mdc:app/globals.css)

### Key Directories

#### Components

- **Location**: `components/`
- **UI Components**: [components/ui/](mdc:components/ui/)
- **Feature Components**: [components/timer.tsx](mdc:components/timer.tsx), [components/task-list.tsx](mdc:components/task-list.tsx)
- **Specialized**: [components/version-display.tsx](mdc:components/version-display.tsx), [components/sync-status.tsx](mdc:components/sync-status.tsx)

#### Libraries & Utilities

- **Core Logic**: [lib/](mdc:lib/)
- **Context Providers**: [lib/timer-context.tsx](mdc:lib/timer-context.tsx), [lib/task-context.tsx](mdc:lib/task-context.tsx)
- **Version Management**: [lib/version.ts](mdc:lib/version.ts)
- **Performance**: [lib/utils/performance.ts](mdc:lib/utils/performance.ts)

#### Scripts & Automation

- **Auto-Versioning**: [scripts/auto-version.js](mdc:scripts/auto-version.js)
- **Pre-commit Hooks**: [scripts/pre-commit-version.js](mdc:scripts/pre-commit-version.js)
- **Performance Testing**: [scripts/performance-analysis.js](mdc:scripts/performance-analysis.js)

#### Testing

- **Test Structure**: `__tests__/`
- **Component Tests**: [**tests**/components/](mdc:__tests__/components/)
- **Integration Tests**: [**tests**/integration/](mdc:__tests__/integration/)
- **Utility Tests**: [**tests**/lib/](mdc:__tests__/lib/)

#### Documentation

- **Guides**: [docs/guides/](mdc:docs/guides/)
- **Performance**: [docs/guides/PERFORMANCE_OPTIMIZATIONS.md](mdc:docs/guides/PERFORMANCE_OPTIMIZATIONS.md)
- **Auto-Versioning**: [docs/guides/AUTO_VERSIONING.md](mdc:docs/guides/AUTO_VERSIONING.md)

## Key Features

### 1. **Auto-Versioning System**

- Real-time file watching and version tracking
- Git integration with pre-commit hooks
- Build number and change count tracking
- Comprehensive version display

### 2. **Performance Optimizations**

- localStorage access caching
- Console logging reduction
- Component memoization
- Performance monitoring utilities

### 3. **Testing Strategy**

- Comprehensive test coverage
- Integration tests for key workflows
- Performance testing
- Visual regression testing

### 4. **Development Workflow**

- Auto-versioning during development
- Performance monitoring
- Organized commit strategy
- Continuous testing

## Development Commands

### Core Development

```bash
npm run dev              # Standard development
npm run dev:watch        # Development with auto-versioning
npm run build           # Production build
npm run start           # Production server
```

### Version Management

```bash
npm run version:init    # Initialize version tracking
npm run version:watch   # Start file watcher
npm run version:status  # Check current version
npm run version:reset   # Reset version tracking
```

### Testing

```bash
npm test               # Run all tests
npm run test:watch     # Watch mode testing
npm run test:coverage  # Coverage report
```

### Performance

```bash
npm run lighthouse     # Lighthouse performance tests
npm run performance    # Performance analysis
```

## File Naming Conventions

### Components

- **PascalCase**: `TimerComponent.tsx`
- **Feature-based**: `timer.tsx`, `task-list.tsx`
- **UI Components**: `ui/button.tsx`, `ui/dialog.tsx`

### Utilities

- **camelCase**: `version.ts`, `performance.ts`
- **kebab-case**: `auto-version.js`, `pre-commit-version.js`

### Tests

- **Component**: `component-name.test.tsx`
- **Integration**: `feature-integration.test.tsx`
- **Utilities**: `utility-name.test.ts`

## Import Patterns

### Absolute Imports

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Use absolute imports
import { TimerProvider } from "@/lib/timer-context";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { getVersionInfo } from "@/lib/version";
```

### Relative Imports

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Use relative for closely related files
import { TimerDisplay } from "./timer-display";
import { useTimer } from "../hooks/use-timer";
```

## State Management

### Context Providers

- **Timer State**: [lib/timer-context.tsx](mdc:lib/timer-context.tsx)
- **Task State**: [lib/task-context.tsx](mdc:lib/task-context.tsx)
- **Theme State**: [lib/theme-context.tsx](mdc:lib/theme-context.tsx)
- **Auth State**: [lib/auth-context.tsx](mdc:lib/auth-context.tsx)

### Local Storage

- **Version Data**: `pomofit-*` keys
- **User Preferences**: `pomofit-settings`
- **Task Data**: `pomofit-tasks`
- **History Data**: `pomofit-history`

